# Everything here is LF, in the index and in the working tree.
#
# This is not a style preference. `cargo package` reads the working tree rather
# than the index, so a source file that drifted to CRLF changes the published
# crate's SHA-256 while `git status` stays silent about it -- a path git itself
# checked out as CRLF still matches the stat data cached in the index, so status
# never reads its contents. `git ls-files --eol` is what shows the real state.
* text eol=lf
